        "title": "Woody API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Fetch random photos of Woody the cat over a tiny CORS-enabled REST API",
        "homepage": "https://woody.cat",
        "docs_url": "https://woody.cat",
        "about_md": "Woody API is a small public REST service that serves photos of Woody, a cat. It is hosted at [woody.cat](https://woody.cat) and exposes its image endpoints under the `purr.woody.cat` subdomain.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- A random Woody photo via `GET https://purr.woody.cat`\n- A specific photo by ID via `GET https://purr.woody.cat/{id}` (for example, `GET https://purr.woody.cat/1`)\n\nBoth endpoints are CORS-enabled, so the service can be called directly from browser-side code. According to the [freepublicapis.com listing](https://freepublicapis.com/woody-api), the API requires no authentication and has been reliably available with sub-second response times.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "api": "Top-level grouping for the Woody photo service hosted at `https://purr.woody.cat`.",
          "random": "A randomly selected Woody photo returned by `GET https://purr.woody.cat`, or a specific one via `GET https://purr.woody.cat/{id}`."
        },
        "auth": false
